{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q7041494","formula":"C₁₅H₂₉NO₂","hill":"C15H29NO2","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":15.0,"H":29.0,"N":1.0,"O":2.0},"names":{"en":"Nitropentadecene"},"descriptions":{"en":"Nitropentadecene, or more precisely (E)-1-nitropentadec-1-ene, is a highly toxic unsaturated nitroalkene, the only aliphatic nitro compound known to be synthesized by insects. It is produced by termite soldiers of genus Prorhinotermes (Isoptera, Rhinotermitidae) as a defensive chemical. Nitropentadecene is biosynthesized and stored in one of the exocrine glands, a frontal gland, of termite soldiers, and it is released upon attack of enemy."},"fame":4,"pubchemCid":14753110,"mass":255.4,"charge":0,"smiles":"CCCCCCCCCCCCC/C=C/[N+](=O)[O-]","inchikey":"VXUKZOXLZJQOHU-CCEZHUSRSA-N","iupac":"(E)-1-nitropentadec-1-ene","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"14753110","atoms":47,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":8.123,"y":-0.783,"z":1.073,"el":"O"},{"x":8.888,"y":-1.043,"z":-0.976,"el":"O"},{"x":8.035,"y":-0.663,"z":-0.159,"el":"N"},{"x":-2.942,"y":0.573,"z":-0.04,"el":"C"},{"x":-1.601,"y":0.0,"z":0.431,"el":"C"},{"x":-4.144,"y":-0.284,"z":0.366,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.392,"y":0.813,"z":-0.037,"el":"C"},{"x":-5.479,"y":0.248,"z":-0.166,"el":"C"},{"x":0.92,"y":0.154,"z":0.397,"el":"C"},{"x":-6.72,"y":-0.58,"z":0.18,"el":"C"},{"x":2.131,"y":0.943,"z":-0.103,"el":"C"},{"x":-8.026,"y":0.037,"z":-0.323,"el":"C"},{"x":3.443,"y":0.264,"z":0.304,"el":"C"},{"x":-9.229,"y":-0.828,"z":0.058,"el":"C"},{"x":4.685,"y":1.036,"z":-0.152,"el":"C"},{"x":-10.534,"y":-0.203,"z":-0.41,"el":"C"},{"x":5.97,"y":0.358,"z":0.228,"el":"C"},{"x":6.87,"y":-0.042,"z":-0.672,"el":"C"},{"x":-3.064,"y":1.585,"z":0.365,"el":"H"},{"x":-2.924,"y":0.669,"z":-1.132,"el":"H"},{"x":-1.599,"y":-0.058,